# One deployment environment's credentials, for scripts/secrets/set-environment.sh.
#
#   cp environment.env.example qa.env      # then fill it in
#   ./set-environment.sh qa qa.env         # dry run — names and digests, no values
#   ./set-environment.sh qa qa.env --apply
#   rm qa.env
#
# Delete the file afterwards. It holds passwords in plain text; dev.env, qa.env,
# stage.env and prod.env are all in .gitignore for that reason.
#
# Use the plain names below whichever environment this is. The script adds the
# environment prefix when it writes to the vault, so MAINDB_PASSWORD in qa.env
# becomes `trd365-qa-maindb-password`. That prefix is the whole point: it is what
# stops a QA credential from ever being served to a utility running against prod.
#
# The script asks trd365_core.environments what each environment needs, so a
# field this one does not use is reported as ignored rather than silently
# accepted. What it needs today:
#
#   Dev, QA   maindb + orgdb dbname and password           (4 values, direct)
#   Stage     the same, plus the bastion password          (6 values)
#   Prod      already configured — nothing to do here
#
# Anything left blank that the environment requires stops the run and is named.

# --- Main application database ---------------------------------------------
MAINDB_DBNAME=
MAINDB_PASSWORD=

# --- Organisation database -------------------------------------------------
ORGDB_DBNAME=
ORGDB_PASSWORD=

# --- SSH bastion (Stage and Prod only; Dev and QA are reached directly) -----
# The host and account are in the code — 172.203.151.166 as thinkrd_DevOps,
# shared by both. Only the password is needed here.
MAINDB_SSH_PASSWORD=
ORGDB_SSH_PASSWORD=

# --- TRD365 AI database ----------------------------------------------------
# Prod only so far. Whether Dev, QA and Stage have their own instance is an open
# question; until the code knows a server for one, these are ignored.
TRD365AI_DBNAME=
TRD365AI_PASSWORD=

# --- Overriding the topology (rare) ----------------------------------------
# Servers, ports, users, sslmode and the bastion address live in
# trd365_core.environments, reviewable in git. Uncomment one here only to
# override it without a release — useful mid-diagnosis, and worth removing after.
#
# MAINDB_HOST=
# MAINDB_PORT=5432
# MAINDB_USER=
# MAINDB_SSLMODE=require
# MAINDB_SSH_HOST=
# MAINDB_SSH_PORT=22
# MAINDB_SSH_USER=
# ORGDB_HOST=
# ORGDB_PORT=5432
# ORGDB_USER=
# ORGDB_SSLMODE=require
# ORGDB_SSH_HOST=
# ORGDB_SSH_PORT=22
# ORGDB_SSH_USER=
# TRD365AI_HOST=
# TRD365AI_PORT=5432
# TRD365AI_USER=
# TRD365AI_SSLMODE=prefer
